  "narrative": "<h3 class=\"story-subheading\">Short impact summary</h3>\n<p class=\"story-text\">FDX1 DMS - Tsvekov lab (2025) in Figshare. 1 documented downstream reuse(s).</p>\n<h3 class=\"story-subheading\">Full narrative</h3>\n<p class=\"story-text\">FDX1 DMS - Tsvekov lab (2025) in Figshare is authored by Kwon, Jason. Topics: Raw material, Raw data, Environmental science, Computer science and Table (database).</p>\n<p class=\"story-text\">No citations yet.</p>\n<p class=\"story-text\">Limited online visibility beyond citations.</p>",
  "provenance": {},
  "story_type": "DataStory",
  "publisher": "Digital Science",
  "narrative_llm": "<h3 class=\"story-subheading\">Short impact summary</h3>\n<p class=\"story-text\">This open Figshare dataset for the Tsvekov lab\u2019s FDX1 DMS work is still early in its documented impact profile, but it already shows one downstream reuse in a biomedical article. The record also shows light direct use, with 5 views and no recorded downloads.</p>\n<h3 class=\"story-subheading\">Full narrative</h3>\n<p class=\"story-text\">FDX1 DMS - Tsvekov lab is a 2025 open dataset deposited on Figshare by Jason Kwon. The materials are described as raw sequencing reads from FDX1 deep mutational scanning screens, with processed analyses available separately in a linked code repository. In the current record, the dataset is openly accessible through multiple repository instances and is associated with a small but concrete usage footprint.</p>\n<p class=\"story-text\">The strongest evidence of impact is reuse: the dataset has one documented downstream mention in the biomedical literature, indicating that it has already been incorporated into at least one research article. That kind of reuse is a meaningful early signal for a data resource, especially for a dataset intended to support analysis and follow-on interpretation rather than stand alone as a narrative publication.</p>\n<p class=\"story-text\">Beyond that reuse signal, the visible engagement remains modest. The dataset has 5 recorded views and no recorded downloads in the available DataCite metrics, while OpenAlex lists 0 citations for the record. Scite also shows no citation activity, and there are no recorded event-data mentions in the archive available here. Together, these counts suggest a quiet but emerging usage profile rather than broad dissemination at this stage.</p>\n<p class=\"story-text\">The subject tagging points to a computational and engineering-oriented data resource centered on raw data and processing workflows, consistent with the dataset\u2019s role in a sequencing-based screening project. The absence of a richer public-discourse record should be interpreted cautiously: some channels are simply not captured for all works, so the evidence here describes what is documented rather than the full extent of possible use.</p>\n<p class=\"story-text\">Overall, the record shows a clearly open dataset with one confirmed scholarly reuse and limited direct traffic so far. Its impact story is therefore best understood as early-stage but real: a reusable experimental data resource that has already entered the biomedical literature, even though broader citation and attention indicators have not yet accumulated.</p>",
  "narrative_source": "template"
